  "generated_text": "Given that \\( p(x) = Ax^5 + Bx^3 + Cx + 4 \\) is divided by \\( x - 3 \\) and the remainder is 11, we can use the Remainder Theorem. According to the Remainder Theorem,\n p\\[ p) = 11\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\( p(x) \\) is divided by \\( x + 3 \\).\n\nUsing the Remainder Theorem again, we know that the remainder when \\( p(x) \\) is divided by \\( x + 3 \\) is the same as \\( p(-)) \\\n\nSo, we need to find \\( p(-3) \\):\n\n\\[(-(-3) = A3)^)^5 B B333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( p(x) \\) is divided by \\( x + 3 \\) is:\n\n\\boxed{-7}",
  "grade": {
